[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186132373 :answer-field/choices 17592186132374] [:db/retract 17592186132373 :answer-field/choices 17592186132375] [:db/retract 17592186132373 :answer-field/choices 17592186132376] [:db/retract 17592186132373 :answer-field/choices 17592186132377] [:db/retract 17592186132373 :answer-field/choices 17592186132378] {:db/id 17592186133807 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-789ea0d3-54ac-52af-9aa3-c806bd076e69"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133616 :question/problem "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ | $2$ |\n\nConsider the data above and the matrices below. Find an expression (in terms of $X$ and $\\mathbf{y}$) for the vector of coefficients $\\boldsymbol{\\beta}$ of the curve $y=\\beta_0 + \\beta_1 x + \\beta_2 x^2 + \\beta_3 x^3$ that best fits the data. \n\n![](images/17/172f8147d4d58d4d3edc42f96e3fb248f59cb749ed0e387c9c8bcddfec08bf79.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-789ea0d3-54ac-52af-9aa3-c806bd076e69" :question/id #uuid "789ea0d3-54ac-52af-9aa3-c806bd076e69" :question/math-academy-id "q-139599" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$2$** | **$4$** | **$6$** | **$8$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $3$ |\n\nConsider the data above and the matrices below. Find an expression for the vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}$ that best fits the data. \n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & {0}^{2} & {0}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 6 & {6}^{2} & {6}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 8 & {8}^{2} & {8}^{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,\\beta =[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\nX\\beta =y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\overset{^}{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b5f5769d-1629-52ad-a8ed-38afe0f42079"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b5f5769d-1629-52ad-a8ed-38afe0f42079" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5f5769d-1629-52ad-a8ed-38afe0f42079" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6ca78b37-8471-59f6-984c-04f09b456143" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a5d7a022-1c16-5e7b-ba63-b8d6ebd79ac5" "answer-ffaf612d-85b8-52f9-bacb-05a3a72950b8" "answer-6ca78b37-8471-59f6-984c-04f09b456143" "answer-28ecf387-c091-569b-870f-de70138cb197" "answer-021af7c8-298c-5829-b9fa-fc8322b9f50d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5d7a022-1c16-5e7b-ba63-b8d6ebd79ac5" :answer/id #uuid "a5d7a022-1c16-5e7b-ba63-b8d6ebd79ac5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(X{X}^{T})^{-1}X{X}^{T}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ffaf612d-85b8-52f9-bacb-05a3a72950b8" :answer/id #uuid "ffaf612d-85b8-52f9-bacb-05a3a72950b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}\\,Xy" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ca78b37-8471-59f6-984c-04f09b456143" :answer/id #uuid "6ca78b37-8471-59f6-984c-04f09b456143" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28ecf387-c091-569b-870f-de70138cb197" :answer/id #uuid "28ecf387-c091-569b-870f-de70138cb197" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "X({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-021af7c8-298c-5829-b9fa-fc8322b9f50d" :answer/id #uuid "021af7c8-298c-5829-b9fa-fc8322b9f50d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "X({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133823 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d9bbc936-cdf8-5bb2-be25-3df4f1bc3232"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d9bbc936-cdf8-5bb2-be25-3df4f1bc3232" :question/id #uuid "d9bbc936-cdf8-5bb2-be25-3df4f1bc3232" :question/math-academy-id "q-139653" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$-3$** | **$-1$** | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $-25$ | $5$ | $20$ | $35$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the observation vector $y$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$-3$** | **$-1$** | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $-25$ | $5$ | $20$ | $35$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & (-3)^{2} \\\\ 1 & -1 & (-1)^{2} \\\\ 1 & 1 & {1}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -25 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 35\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b4aab56a-66ce-5d92-bf05-9bff500864c1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b4aab56a-66ce-5d92-bf05-9bff500864c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4aab56a-66ce-5d92-bf05-9bff500864c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a61433c9-2b22-57c8-9478-14e323e7d6b6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a348d2b4-ce93-5a99-a6ed-1906d407475a" "answer-65dd863d-70c0-5170-aa9a-00b0ab5e1a31" "answer-625975e6-7869-5a67-bc59-519fa2d8371d" "answer-a61433c9-2b22-57c8-9478-14e323e7d6b6" "answer-a6559ef5-d440-5051-9b33-5e541b8f53b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a348d2b4-ce93-5a99-a6ed-1906d407475a" :answer/id #uuid "a348d2b4-ce93-5a99-a6ed-1906d407475a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(-3)^{2} \\\\ (-1)^{2} \\\\ {1}^{2} \\\\ {3}^{2} \\\\ {5}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65dd863d-70c0-5170-aa9a-00b0ab5e1a31" :answer/id #uuid "65dd863d-70c0-5170-aa9a-00b0ab5e1a31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(-5)^{2} \\\\ (-25)^{2} \\\\ {5}^{2} \\\\ {20}^{2} \\\\ {35}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-625975e6-7869-5a67-bc59-519fa2d8371d" :answer/id #uuid "625975e6-7869-5a67-bc59-519fa2d8371d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a61433c9-2b22-57c8-9478-14e323e7d6b6" :answer/id #uuid "a61433c9-2b22-57c8-9478-14e323e7d6b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -25 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 35\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6559ef5-d440-5051-9b33-5e541b8f53b5" :answer/id #uuid "a6559ef5-d440-5051-9b33-5e541b8f53b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134389 :question/problem "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & {1}^{2} & {1}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{2} & {5}^{3}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]